implementationPlan.description:
Add the PR packaging smoke to .github/workflows/ci.yml with the Edit tool (DoD 1). Insert the step immediately after the step "Test VS Code daemon startup". At ff56d4ff that is the last step of job build-all-platforms and the last lines of the file (316-324). Re-read the file end at start_step and plan against HEAD as it stands. The governor dropped the old ci.yml peer edges, so there is nothing to wait for. Add one blank line, then this text verbatim: list items at 6 spaces, keys at 8, the run block at 10.

      - name: Package the VS Code extension and smoke-test its bundle
        # One OS is enough for a packaging smoke. vsce's prepublish re-bundles the daemon and proxy built above, so a
        # .vscodeignore or bundle-manifest.json regression fails the pull request instead of the release.
        if: matrix.os == 'ubuntu-latest'
        shell: bash
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          vsix="$RUNNER_TEMP/moe-vscode.vsix"
          (cd moe-vscode && npm run package -- --out "$vsix")
          unzip -Z1 "$vsix" > "$RUNNER_TEMP/moe-vscode.files"
          # Every bundle-manifest.json target must ship: a file target itself, a directory target every file that
          # bundle-assets.mjs staged under it. Reading the staged copy keeps the exclude rules in the bundler alone.
          node --input-type=module - scripts/bundle-manifest.json "$RUNNER_TEMP/moe-vscode.files" moe-vscode/bundled <<'CHECK'
          import fs from 'node:fs';
          import path from 'node:path';
          const [manifestFile, listingFile, stagedRoot] = process.argv.slice(2);
          const shipped = new Set(fs.readFileSync(listingFile, 'utf8').split('\n').filter(Boolean));
          // As bundle-assets.mjs reads a copy: with `files`, each <into>/<name> is a target; without, the whole <into> directory.
          const { copies } = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(manifestFile, 'utf8'));
          const targets = (Array.isArray(copies) ? copies : []).flatMap(copy => Array.isArray(copy?.files) && copy.files.length > 0
            ? copy.files.map(name => path.posix.join(String(copy.into), String(name))) : [copy?.into]);
          if (shipped.size === 0 || targets.length === 0) {
            console.error(`Nothing to compare: ${shipped.size} vsix entries, ${targets.length} targets in ${manifestFile}`);
            process.exit(1);
          }
          const missing = [];
          for (const to of targets) {
            if (typeof to !== 'string' || !to || path.isAbsolute(to) || to.split('/').includes('..')) { missing.push(`${to} (not bundle-relative)`); continue; }
            const staged = path.join(stagedRoot, to);
            if (!fs.statSync(staged, { throwIfNoEntry: false })?.isDirectory()) {
              if (!shipped.has(`extension/bundled/${to}`)) missing.push(to);
              continue;
            }
            const files = fs.readdirSync(staged, { recursive: true, withFileTypes: true }).filter(entry => entry.isFile())
              .map(entry => path.relative(stagedRoot, path.join(entry.parentPath, entry.name)).split(path.sep).join('/'));
            if (files.length === 0) missing.push(`${to}/ (nothing staged)`);
            for (const file of files) if (!shipped.has(`extension/bundled/${file}`)) missing.push(file);
          }
          for (const item of new Set(missing)) console.error(`Missing from the vsix: extension/bundled/${item}`);
          if (missing.length > 0) process.exit(1);
          console.log(`All ${targets.length} bundle-manifest.json targets are in the vsix`);
          CHECK
          smoke="$RUNNER_TEMP/moe-vscode-smoke"
          unzip -oq "$vsix" -d "$smoke"
          node scripts/tests/onboarding.mjs "$smoke/extension/bundled"

Design notes, not code:
- No npm ci here. The previous step ran `npm ci` and `npm run compile` in moe-vscode, and the job's "Build daemon" and "Build proxy" steps installed and built both packages, as bundle-assets.mjs's fresh-dist check needs. `npm run package` is `vsce package`, whose vscode:prepublish runs bundle-assets.mjs (stages moe-vscode/bundled) and esbuild.
- Targets follow the manifest VSC-16 landed (84536308): `copies[]` of {from, into, files?, required?, exclude?}. They are derived exactly as architect-0fcb7226 fixed in task-6fbd0811's comment: `files ? files.map(n => into + '/' + n) : [into]`. As in bundle-assets.mjs, an empty `files` is a directory copy. Do not add fields to the manifest. Reading the staged copy, not re-applying `exclude`, keeps the Ant exclude rules in the two builds only.
- Order is package, listing, check, unzip, onboarding. The cheap check fails first with a named path. Onboarding is the same command release.yml's "Verify packaged onboarding" and the JetBrains job run.
- Error handling: the check fails closed. It exits 1 with `Nothing to compare:` on an empty listing or no targets; on a target that is not bundle-relative; on a missing file target; and on an empty staged directory or any staged file missing from the vsix. Each such path is printed once as `Missing from the vsix: extension/bundled/<path>`; checkRef 3 greps that exact text, so keep it. An unreadable or malformed manifest throws, Node prints the error and exits 1. bundle-assets.mjs has already refused a malformed manifest before packaging.
- Actions interpolates only `${{ }}`, so the JS `${...}` template literals pass through. The quoted heredoc `<<'CHECK'` stops bash expansion. YAML strips the 10-space block indent, so `CHECK` lands at column 0. Keep every line at the block indent or deeper, with no tabs. Node 24 (setup-node '24') has `readdirSync({ recursive, withFileTypes })` and `Dirent.parentPath`. Write no forbidden token.
- No new script file: DoD 5 limits the diff to the two files.
